ed.\n- The current policy date and why it supersedes the stale policy excerpt.\n- The receipt threshold.\n- The seat-upgrade rule.\n- The lodging cap calculation basis.\n- The meal and alcohol rule.\n- The ride-share tip cap.\n- The supplies receipt rule.\n\n## `answer/expense_decisions.md`\n\nRecord the item-level audit decision for every expense.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every expense ID in `expenses.csv`.\n- For each expense: claimed amount, approved amount, non-reimbursable amount, status (`approved`, `partial`, or `rejected`), and the policy or receipt reason.\n\n## `answer/reimbursement_summary.md`\n\nWrite the final reimbursement summary for the finance teammate.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- Reimbursable total.\n- Non-reimbursable total.\n- Arithmetic showing how the reimbursable total was calculated.\n- Fully approved expense IDs.\n- Partially reimbursed or capped expense IDs.\n- Rejected expense IDs.\n\nRules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n- Use dollar amounts rounded to two decimal places when needed.\n- Extra scratch files are allowed, but scoring is based on the three named deliverables under `answer/`.\n\n---CURRENT POLICY---\n# Current Finance Travel Policy\n\nPolicy date: 2026-04-20\n\nEffective for trips starting on or after 2026-05-01. This policy supersedes older travel policy excerpts for covered trips.\n\nGeneral rules:\n\n- Use this current policy when it conflicts with older policy excerpts.\n- Receipts are required for every expense of $75.00 or more.\n- Expenses without required receipts are not reimbursable when a receipt is required.\n\nAir travel:\n\n- Economy airfare is reimbursable with a receipt.\n- Seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is provided in the receipt evidence. No preapproval means no reimbursement.\n\nLodging:\n\n- Lodging is reimbursable up to $220.00 per night, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees.\n- Apply the cap by multiplying covered nights by $220.00.\n\nMeals:\n\n- Meals are reimbursable at actual cost up to $65.00 per day.\n- Alcohol is not reimbursable and must be removed from meal receipts.\n\nRide-share:\n\n- Ride-share base fare is reimbursable with a receipt.\n- Tips are reimbursable up to 20% of the base fare.\n- Any tip amount above 20% of the base fare is not reimbursable.\n\nSupplies:\n\n- Work supplies can be reimbursed only when a required receipt is provided and the business purpose is clear.\n\nTrip covered by this audit:\n\n- Employee: Jordan Lee\n- Trip dates: 2026-05-08 to 2026-05-10\n- Covered lodging nights: 2\n\n---STALE POLICY---\n# Stale Policy Excerpt\n\nPolicy date: 2026-03-01\n\nThis excerpt was copied into the travel folder before the finance policy update.\n\nOlder rules:\n\n- Receipts are required only for expenses over $100.00.\n- Lodging is reimbursable up to $260.00 per night.\n- Ride-share tips are reimbursable up to 25% of the base fare.\n- Seat upgrades are reimbursable up to $50.00 when booked with economy airfare.\n\nImportant: this excerpt may be stale if a newer policy applies.\n\n---EXPENSES---\nexpense_id,date,category,description,claimed_amount_usd\nT-001,2026-05-08,airfare,Round-trip economy airfare,480.00\nT-002,2026-05-08,airfare,Exit-row seat upgrade,45.00\nT-003,2026-05-08,lodging,Hotel stay for two covered nights,510.00\nT-004,2026-05-09,meal,Team dinner with wine,76.00\nT-005,2026-05-09,rideshare,Airport ride-share with tip,70.00\nT-006,2026-05-10,supplies,USB-C adapters purchased during trip,82.00\nT-007,2026-05-10,meal,Breakfast,18.00\n\n---RECEIPTS---\n# Receipt Evidence\n\n- T-001: Receipt present. Economy round-trip airfare, $480.00.\n- T-002: Receipt present. Exit-row seat upgrade, $45.00. No written preapproval is included.\n- T-003: Receipt present. Hotel folio total $510.00 for two nights, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees.\n- T-004: Receipt present. Food subtotal $58.00 and wine $18.00, total $76.00.\n- T-005: Receipt present. Base fare $50.00 and tip $20.00, total $70.00.\n- T-006: No receipt provided. Business purpose note says \"USB-C adapters for demo room.\"\n- T-007: Receipt present. Breakfast, $18.00."}, {"func_name": "run_in_task", "args": {"command": "mkdir -p answer\ncat > answer/policy_application.md <<'EOF'\n# Policy Application\n\n## Policy-selection checkpoint\n- **Trip dates audited:** 2026-05-08 to 2026-05-10.\n- **Controlling policy source:** `current_policy.md`.\n- **Current policy date:** 2026-04-20.\n- **Why it controls:** The current policy is effective for trips starting on or after 2026-05-01 and explicitly says it supersedes older travel policy excerpts for covered trips. This trip started on 2026-05-08, so the stale excerpt dated 2026-03-01 does not control where there is any conflict.\n\n## Rules applied for this audit\n- **Receipt threshold:** Receipts are required for every expense of **$75.00 or more**. If a required receipt is missing, the expense is not reimbursable.\n- **Seat-upgrade rule:** Seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are **not reimbursable unless written preapproval is provided in the receipt evidence**. No preapproval means no reimbursement.\n- **Lodging cap calculation basis:** Lodging is reimbursable up to **$220.00 per night**, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees. The cap is applied by multiplying covered nights by $220.00. For this trip, **2 covered nights \u00d7 $220.00 = $440.00** maximum lodging reimbursement.\n- **Meal and alcohol rule:** Meals are reimbursable at actual cost up to **$65.00 per day**. **Alcohol is not reimbursable** and must be removed from meal receipts.\n- **Ride-share tip cap:** Ride-share base fare is reimbursable with a receipt, and **tips are reimbursable only up to 20% of the base fare**. Any tip above that cap is non-reimbursable.\n- **Supplies receipt rule:** Work supplies can be reimbursed only when a **required receipt is provided** and the **business purpose is clear**.\n\n## Item-level audit checkpoint\nItem-by-item application is recorded in `answer/expense_decisions.md`.\n\n## Reimbursement-summary checkpoint\nFinal totals and approval grouping are recorded in `answer/reimbursement_summary.md`.\nEOF\n\ncat > answer/expense_decisions.md <<'EOF'\n# Expense Decisions\n\n| Expense ID | Claimed Amount | Approved Amount | Non-reimbursable Amount | Status | Policy / receipt reason |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---|\n| T-001 | $480.00 | $480.00 | $0.00 | approved | Economy airfare is reimbursable with a receipt. Receipt present. |\n| T-002 | $45.00 | $0.00 | $45.00 | rejected | Seat upgrade is not reimbursable without written preapproval. Receipt is present, but no written preapproval is included. |\n| T-003 | $510.00 | $440.00 | $70.00 | partial | Lodging cap is $220.00 per night for 2 covered nights = $440.00 max. Receipt present; amount above cap is not reimbursable. |\n| T-004 | $76.00 | $58.00 | $18.00 | partial | Meal receipt shows $58.00 food and $18.00 wine. Alcohol is not reimbursable. Approved food amount remains within the $65.00 daily meal cap. |\n| T-005 | $70.00 | $60.00 | $10.00 | partial | Ride-share receipt shows $50.00 base fare and $20.00 tip. Tip cap is 20% of base fare = $10.00, so approved total is $50.00 + $10.00 = $60.00. |\n| T-006 | $82.00 | $0.00 | $82.00 | rejected | Supplies require a receipt when the expense is $75.00 or more. Business purpose is noted, but no receipt was provided, so the expense is not reimbursable. |\n| T-007 | $18.00 | $18.00 | $0.00 | approved | Meal receipt present. Breakfast is reimbursable and remains within the $65.00 daily meal cap for 2026-05-10. |\nEOF\n\ncat > answer/reimbursement_summary.md <<'EOF'\n# Reimbursement Summary\n\n## Final totals\n- **Reimbursable total:** **$1,056.00**\n- **Non-reimbursable total:** **$225.00**\n\n## Arithmetic checkpoint\nReimbursable total calculation:\n- T-001: $480.00\n- T-002: $0.00\n- T-003: $440.00\n- T-004: $58.00\n- T-005: $60.00\n- T-006: $0.00\n- T-007: $18.00\n\n**Total reimbursable = $480.00 + $0.00 + $440.00 + $58.00 + $60.00 + $0.00 + $18.00 = $1,056.00**\n\nNon-reimbursable total calculation:\n- T-001: $0.00\n- T-002: $45.00\n- T-003: $70.00\n- T-004: $18.00\n- T-005: $10.00\n- T-006: $82.00\n- T-007: $0.00\n\n**Total non-reimbursable = $45.00 + $70.00 + $18.00 + $10.00 + $82.00 = $225.00**\n\n## Approval grouping\n- **Fully approved expense IDs:** T-001, T-007\n- **Partially reimbursed or capped expense IDs:** T-003, T-004, T-005\n- **Rejected expense IDs:** T-002, T-006\n\n## Finance note\nThe audit used the current policy dated 2026-04-20 because the trip began on 2026-05-08, which is on or after the 2026-05-01 effective date. The stale policy excerpt was not used where it conflicted with the current policy.\nEOF\n\nprintf '\\n---VERIFY---\\n' && ls -la answer && printf '\\n---FILES---\\n' && for f in answer/policy_application.md answer/expense_decisions.md answer/reimbursement_summary.md; do echo \"FILE: $f\"; test -f \"$f\" && echo PRESENT; done", "timeout_seconds": 60}, "result": "---VERIFY---\ntotal 24\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 5 douglas  staff   160 Jun 15 19:42 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 9 douglas  staff   288 Jun 15 19:40 ..\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 douglas  staff  1366 Jun 15 19:42 expense_decisions.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 douglas  staff  1923 Jun 15 19:42 policy_application.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 douglas  staff  1043 Jun 15 19:42 reimbursement_summary.md\n\n---FILES---\nFILE: answer/policy_application.md\nPRESENT\nFILE: answer/expense_decisions.md\nPRESENT\nFILE: answer/reimbursement_summary.md\nPRESENT"}], "usage": {"requests": 3, "tool_calls": 3, "input_tokens": 6582, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "input_audio_tokens": 0, "cache_audio_read_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 1729, "output_audio_tokens": 0, "total_tokens": 8311, "details": {}}, "cost": {"usd": null, "es